 Each Cargo invocation is recorded before the adapter execs the actual wrapper. Same-PID compiler-boundary records must match the complete original argv plus only the existing routing suffix and the fixed eligible host O3/MIR1/LTO-off/check suffix. Both arms must have identical original Cargo argv after replacing their explicit output-directory prefix; crate metadata, extra filenames and extern names are included in this comparison. Build-script values must match exactly and both actual target tests must pass. Actual extern artifact hashes are retained; native binary equality is not assumed.
 
 The source and physical tool binding is prepared separately after the candidate files are complete. The initial state is unbound and unrun. The driver requires a fresh output namespace and holds the canonical workload lock. It reuses the previous real fixture's observed 30-second command and 256 MiB output thresholds, waits normally on a breach, and retains the failure. It uses no process signals and makes no reservation or hard quota claim.
+
+The first run built the real wrapper and passed the off-arm native test, then its checker rejected Cargo's valid pathless `--extern proc_macro`. Run 01 and every source/receipt are retained. This successor accepts that exact builtin only in the host proc-macro unit; other pathless externs still fail. New work/results namespaces prevent overwriting the failed check.
